-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",96,{
[3041]="70048C51\n1\tTravel to the Isenmouthe in the fortress of Carach Angren\tThe Isenmouthe is the gate between Udûn and Dor Amarth, and it is built into the fortress of Carach Angren.\n2\tPass through the Isenmouthe and find Brungos in Dor Amarth\tBrungos is on the other side of the Isenmouthe, in Dor Amarth.\n3\tTalk to Brungos in Dor Amarth\tBrungos is in a small ruined settlement in Dor Amarth.\n4\tDefeat enemies in Dor Amarth (total: 12)\tFierce enemies stalk the Doomfold of Dor Amarth, and Brungos asked for your help defeating them.\n5\tTalk to Brungos in Dor Amarth\tBrungos is in a small ruined settlement in Dor Amarth.\n6\tFind Covadil near Lûghash, in Dor Amarth\tCovadil went north-east in Dor Amarth, intending to see Lûghash.\n7\tTalk to Covadil near Lûghash\tThe Gondorian scholar Covadil is near the Spire of Lûghash, in Dor Amarth.\n8\tDig in the ash piles outside Lûghash (total: 6)\tCovadil asked you to search among the old ash piles outside Lûghash for some sign of the Gondorian presence.\n9\tBring the broken metal pieces to Covadil near Lûghash\tThe Gondorian scholar Covadil is near the Spire of Lûghash, in Dor Amarth.\n",
[3042]="70056FAC\n1\tMeet up with Glóin at the rocky spur on which stands the ruins of Framsburg\tGlóin directed you to meet up with him on the rocky spur to the west, on which stands the old town of Framsburg, from where the forebears of the Rohirrim once hailed.\n2\tTalk to Glóin on the Framsburg side of the bridge\tGlóin is on the rocky spur on which stands the ruins of Framsburg.\n3\tDefeat creatures near the ruins of Framsburg (total: 8)\030Explore the north-east side of the Framsburg promontory\030Explore the northern ruins on the Framsburg promontory\030Find some disturbed earth among the ruins of Framsburg\tDrakes, worms, and other creatures have taken up residence within the ruins of Framsburg, and Glóin thinks you should defeat the creatures while you search within Framsburg for some sign of the Gundabad raiding-party.\n4\tBring the thundercloud badge to Glóin on the eastern side of the Framsburg promontory\tGlóin is on the rocky spur on which stands the ruins of Framsburg. The old dwarf will be interested in the metal badge you discovered.\n5\tFind more tracks somewhere to the south, along the river\tGlóin believes the Orc raiding-party scouted its path from the Framsburg promontory and continued south, following the river.\n6\tTalk to Imák by the tracks south of Framsburg\tImák stands by the tracks he found south of Framsburg.\n",
[3043]="70064BDC\n1\tTalk to Sirgon on the eastern docks of Pelargir, in King's Gondor\tSirgon stands along the eastern docks of Pelargir, in King's Gondor.\n2\tDefeat brigand toughs on the western side of Pelargir, King's Gondor (total: 8)\tBrigand toughs on the western side of Pelargir have made problems for Sirgon's shipbuilders, and he wants you to help his son Faltharan deal with them.\n3\tTalk to Faltharan north-west of the auction house in Pelargir, King's Gondor\tFaltharan is to the north-west of the auction house in Pelargir, King's Gondor.\n4\tFind King Elessar and Sirgon at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, King's Gondor\tKing Elessar and Sirgon are overseeing ship repairs in south-eastern Pelargir, King's Gondor.\n5\tTalk to King Elessar at the dry dock in Pelargir, King's Gondor\tKing Elessar is at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, King's Gondor.\n",
[3044]="70048C52\n1\tTalk to Thorvíl on the road east of Lûghash\030Talk to Fairanc on the road east of Lûghash\tA number of soldiers are hurrying down the road towards Lûghash.\n2\tTalk to Covadil on the road east of Lûghash\tCovadil has come up to the group of soldiers on the road east of Lûghash.\n3\tFind Rhogrin on the road to the great abyss east of Lûghash\tRhogrin is near the great abyss east of the Spire of Lûghash, in Dor Amarth.\n4\tTalk to Rhogrin on the road to the great abyss\tRhogrin stands near the great abyss in Dor Amarth.\n5\tTalk to Rhogrin on the road to the great abyss\tRhogrin is standing on the road to the great abyss in Dor Amarth, and seems to be himself again.\n6\tTalk to Covadil on the road east of Lûghash\tCovadil is on the road east of Lûghash.\n7\tTalk to Mithrandir outside the Black Gate\tMithrandir is outside the Black Gate.\n",
[3045]="70064BE2\n1\tTalk to Queen Arwen at the dry dock in Pelargir, King's Gondor\tQueen Arwen is at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, in King's Gondor.\n2\tTalk to Gimli at the dry dock in Pelargir, King's Gondor\tGimli is at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, in King's Gondor.\n3\tTravel to the entrance of Furukzahar in the White Mountains north of Pelargir, in King's Gondor\tSékhel stands guard outside the entrance to Furukzahar.\n4\tTalk to Sékhel at the entrance to Furukzahar\tThe dwarf Sékhel stands guard at the entrance to Furukzahar.\n5\tTalk to King Elessar outside the entrance to Furukzahar, in King's Gondor\tKing Elessar stands outside the entrance to the Temámir fortress of Furukzahar, in the White Mountains.\n6\tHunt animals in the valley outside Furukzahar (total: 6)\tThe Dwarves of Furukzahar expect a gift from those who visit them, and the guard Sékhel suggested that you hunt the game to be found in the valley for that purpose.\n7\tBring the gifts of meat to Sékhel at the entrance to Furukzahar\tThe dwarf Sékhel stands guard at the entrance to Furukzahar.\n8\tWait until Sékhel says King Elessar is permitted inside Furukzahar\tSékhel, the guard outside Furukzahar, has regretfully informed you that King Elessar is not yet permitted inside. He will have to wait a little longer.\n9\tTalk to Gimli outside the entrance to Furukzahar\tGimli has grown impatient and is not pleased at being made to wait outside the entrance to Furukzahar.\n10\tWait until Sékhel says King Elessar is permitted inside Furukzahar\tSékhel, the guard outside Furukzahar, has regretfully informed you that King Elessar is not yet permitted inside. He will have to wait a little longer.\n11\tTalk to Kutúkh at the entrance to Furukzahar\tKutúkh has emerged from the stronghold of Furukzahar.\n",
[3046]="70056FAD\n1\tImák wants you to follow the river southward in search of the raiding-party.\t\n2\tBy Hengi's Leap you found more tracks left by the raiding-party, but the broken bridge likely prevented them from crossing the river. They may have continued south instead.\t\n3\tFind the source of the blood-spattered tracks\tBloody tracks led eastward, away from the river.\n4\tTravel toward the town of Limlók, to the north-east\tThrúgord spoke of a village of 'Bear-folk' to which the raiding-party planned to go. He must have meant the town of Limlók, to the north-east.\n5\tTalk to Venko in view of Limlók\tVenko looks out upon the Beorning village of Limlók, the obvious question on his lips: where is the raiding-party?\n",
[3047]="70048C53\n1\tTalk to Yadêphal at the Black Gate\tYadêphal has come to the Black Gate, an emissary from his master.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn at the Black Gate\tAragorn is at the Black Gate.\n3\tTalk to Yadêphal and meet with Dulgabêth\tYadêphal is at the Black Gate, waiting to bring Aragorn to treat with his master.\n4\tTalk to Aragorn at the Black Gate\tAragorn is waiting at the Black Gate to hear the terms of Dulgabêth's peace.\n5\tTalk to Yadêphal at the Black Gate\tYadêphal, emissary of Dulgabêth, is at the Black Gate.\n6\tTalk to Aragorn at the Black Gate\tAragorn is at the Black Gate.\n",
[3048]="70064BE3\n1\tFind Hámisar in the throne room of Furukzahar\tThe ruler of Furukzahar awaits you and the King of Gondor in his throne room in the north-western reaches of the fortress.\n2\tTalk to Hámisar inside the throne room of Furukzahar\tHámisar rules Furukzahar from his throne room in the north-western reaches of the fortress.\n3\tExplore the armoury of Furukzahar\030Explore the kitchens of Furukzahar\030Explore the rooms south of the throne room in Furukzahar\030Talk to Asitám in Furukzahar\030Talk to Gúlkhu in Furukzahar\030Talk to Zimikál in Furukzahar\tHámisar has invited you to meet the people of Furukzahar while he speaks with King Elessar.\n4\tTalk to King Elessar in the throne room of Furukzahar\tKing Elessar and Hámisar of the Temámir speak together in the throne room of Furukzahar.\n5\tTalk to Hámisar in the throne room of Furukzahar\tKing Elessar and Hámisar of the Temámir speak together in the throne room of Furukzahar.\n",
[3049]="70056FAF\n1\tTalk to Venko and search Limlók for the vanished raiding-party\tVenko does not believe that Limlók is safe, and the Zhélruka warrior wants to investigate.\n2\tTalk to Imák in Limlók\tImák stands in the centre of Limlók, satisfied with the day's fighting.\n",
[3050]="70056FB7\n1\tJoin Glóin at the edge of Limlók\tGlóin has walked away from your companions and stands now at the edge of Limlók, deep in thought. What troubles the old dwarf?\n2\tTalk to Glóin at the edge of Limlók\tGlóin has walked away from your companions and stands now at the edge of Limlók, deep in thought.\n3\tReturn to Runerik Knotbeard in the village of Limlók\tRunerik Knotbeard stands in the village of Limlók.\n4\tTalk to Runerik Knotbeard in Limlók.\tRunerik Knotbeard stands in the village of Limlók.\n5\tTalk to Venko in Limlók\030Talk to Imák in Limlók\tImák stands in the village of Limlók.\n6\tTalk to Glóin in Limlók\tGlóin has returned to Limlók.\n",
[3051]="70064BE4\n1\tTalk to King Elessar in the throne room of Furukzahar\tKing Elessar is in the throne room of Furukzahar.\n2\tFind the guest rooms provided for Elessar's party on the eastern side of Furukzahar\tThe guest rooms of Furukzahar are on the eastern side of the fortress.\n3\tTalk to King Elessar in the guest rooms of Furukzahar\030Talk to Gimli in the guest rooms of Furukzahar\030Talk to Caebar in the guest rooms of Furukzahar\tKing Elessar's small travelling party waits in the guest rooms provided by Hámisar.\n4\tInvestigate the suspicious door south of the throne room in Furukzahar\tYou experienced a sensation of dread near a door located south of the throne room in Furukzahar, and King Elessar thinks you should investigate further.\n5\tTalk to Gangur Farwend by the suspicious door in Furukzahar\tGangur Farwend, a Longbeard visiting from the north, has quietly called for your attention.\n6\tTalk to Gangur Farwend inside the armoury of Furukzahar in the north-eastern reaches of the fortress\tGangur Farwend has information for you, but he will only share it if you meet with him inside the armoury of Furukzahar.\n7\tTalk to King Elessar in the guest rooms of Furukzahar\tKing Elessar is in the guest rooms of Furukzahar on the eastern side of the fortress.\n8\tExamine the sketch of Khôltekh the Cunning\tElessar gave you the sketch Caebar made of Khôltekh the Cunning from Gangur's description.\n9\tReturn the sketch of Khôltekh the Cunning to Caebar in the guest rooms of Furukzahar\tCaebar is in the guest rooms of Furukzahar.\n10\tTalk to King Elessar in the guest rooms of Furukzahar\tKing Elessar is in the guest rooms of Furukzahar on the eastern side of the fortress.\n",
[3052]="70064BE9\n1\tTalk to Hámisar in the throne room of Furukzahar\tHámisar is in the throne room of Furukzahar.\n2\tTalk to King Elessar in the throne room of Furukzahar\tKing Elessar is in the throne room of Furukzahar.\n3\tRejoin Elessar's travelling party outside the Hall of Ost Anglebed\tThe Hall of Ost Anglebed is to be found south-west of Furukzahar, in King's Gondor.\n4\tTalk to Glindor outside the Hall of Ost Anglebed\tThe Hall of Ost Anglebed is to be found south-west of Furukzahar, in King's Gondor.\n",
[3053]="70064BEA\n1\tYou should ask around Ost Anglebed and learn if anyone knows where the Elf-queen has gone.\t\n2\tFind Queen Arwen in King's Gondor\tIoreth told you she saw someone wearing a cloak much like Queen Arwen's walking to the north-west of Ost Anglebed, in the direction of the river.\n3\tTalk to Queen Arwen\tQueen Arwen is deep in conversation with Roamingstar, north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.\n4\tTalk to Roamingstar, Maiden of the Gilrain\tRoamingstar stands beside Queen Arwen, north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.\n5\tWait for a new arrival\tRoamingstar stands beside Queen Arwen, north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.\n6\tTalk to King Elessar north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor\tKing Elessar has rejoined his Queen north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.\n",
[3054]="70047B48\n1\tFind Pippin in Bâr Thorenion\tYou should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn\030Talk to Éomer\tBoth Aragorn and Éomer can be found outside of the Black Gate, in the area of the Slag Hills. Merry and Pippin have asked you to ask Aragorn and Éomer for permission to venture into Mordor.\n3\tGandalf has appeared nearby to Aragorn and Éomer, outside the Black Gate in the Slag Hills, and has made it clear that he wishes to talk to you.\t\n4\tReturn to Merry and Pippin\tYou should return to Merry and Pippin in Bâr Thorenion with word that they have Aragorn and Éomer's blessings to go into Mordor.\n5\tMeet at the Udûn Foothold\tYou should meet Merry and Pippin at the Foothold encampment in Udûn.\n6\tExplore to the cross-roads\tYou should explore down in the Udûn valley, as far as the first cross-roads, with Merry and Pippin. If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.\n7\tExplore to the soldiers' camps\tYou should explore further along the main road in the Udûn valley, where the mass of soldiers' tents begins. If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.\n8\tLook for a northward path ahead\tMerry has suggested going a bit further along the main road in the Udûn valley, and then look for a way that turns north. If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.\n9\tTalk to Pippin\tYou should talk to Pippin, who says his stomach is growling. If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.\n10\tStop for a bite to eat\tPippin has suggested moving to a flat spot just north of the main road in Udûn, and stopping to eat some and rest up. If you should get separated from Pippin or Merry, use their horns to call them back to you.\n11\tSit down and share in the meal\tYou should sit down with Pippin and Merry at their Mordor picnic spread, off the main road in Udûn, and share in the meal.\n12\tTalk to Merry\tYou should talk to Merry, at the picnic spread in Udûn, and find out what startled him.\n13\tLook for the source of the sound\tGo up the northern path from the hobbits' picnic in Udûn and see if you can find what Merry heard.\n14\tThree travel-worn half-orcs stand on the ledge above you, north of the main road in Udûn, talking amongst themselves. You should listen to hear some more.\t\n15\tThree travel-worn half-orcs stand on the ledge above you, north of the main road in Udûn, talking amongst themselves. You should continue to listen listen to their conversation.\t\n16\tTalk to Merry\030Talk to Pippin\tPippin and Merry are north of the main road in Udûn. You should talk to Merry and Pippin about the trio of half-orcs you just overheard.\n",
[3055]="70014668\n1\tCollect Treasure-coffer (total: 6)\tZabadgathol is in Nud-melek. Glúmur has asked you to return to Zabadgathol, Mazog's fortress within Nud-melek, and to search the area for treasure coffers that might point to the identity of his mysterious ally.\n2\tBring treasure coffers to Bori\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek. You have recovered some treasure coffers from Zabadgathol and should bring them to Bori for his examination.\n",
[3056]="7001424C\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Zelem-melek or the Redhorn Lodes (total: 12)\tOrcs can be found throughout Zelem-melek and the Redhorn Lodes of Moria. Brogur has asked you to defeat Orcs throughout Zelem-melek and the Redhorn Lodes, no matter what tribe to which they belong.\n2\tTalk to Brogur\tBrogur is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek. You have defeated many of the Orcs in Moria, and should report now to Brogur of your success.\n",
[3057]="7000F0CA\n1\tDefeat spying crebain (total: 4)\030Collect jagged talons (total: 4)\tSpying crebain can be found along the banks of the dried-up Sirannon, south-east of the ruined gate in the area near the Walls of Moria. Tulk has asked you to defeat the spying crebain along the banks of the Sirannon and to bring him their talons, which can be put to various uses.\n2\tBring jagged talons to Tulk\tTulk can be found east of the ruined gate in the area near the Walls of Moria. The dwarf Tulk awaits your return with the talons you collected from the spying crebain along the Sirannon.\n",
[3058]="7001474F\n1\tComplete the 'Goblin-slayer' deed in Moria\030Complete the 'Orc-slayer' deed in Moria\tHaldir is at his camp on the boundary of Lothlórien. Haldir has asked you to provide proofs that you are a foe of the Orcs and goblins of Moria by completing two deeds: slaying many Orcs and goblins in Moria.\n2\tTalk to Haldir\tHaldir is at his camp on the boundary of Lothlórien. You have completed two great deeds within Moria, and it could be that the tally of your victories over the Orcs and goblins of Moria will be enough to satisfy Haldir of your intentions.\n",
[3059]="70025371\n1\tTalk to Candaith at the grove east of Lhanuch and experience 'Session: At the Stone of Erech' or read the shortened account instead\tCandaith is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in a grove of trees to the east of the Uch-luth village of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin. Candaith has decided to tell you the story of the Oath-breakers and the Paths of the Dead.\n2\tTalk to Candaith at the grove east of Lhanuch\tCandaith is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in a grove of trees east of the Uch-luth village of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin. You have listened to Candaith relate the tale of the Oath-breakers and the Paths of the Dead and should now speak with him.\n",
[3060]="700145B9\n1\tTalk to Stóthkell\tStóthkell is the dwarf in charge of the Heart of Fire located off the Way of Smiths, among the Silvertine Lodes. Bósi wants you to lend your aid to the dwarves manning the Heart of Fire so they will be prepared if the Orcs attack the Way of Smiths.\n",
[3061]="7002093D\n1\tTalk to Candaith at Weathertop\tCandaith is at his camp in the Lone-lands, at the foot of Weathertop. Elrohir has told you to bring word to the Dúnadan Candaith of the Grey Company's preparations.\n2\tLocate Candaith's hidden cache at Echad Sûl\tCandaith's hidden cache is north-east of his encampment, atop a small rise called Echad Sûl, in the shade of a tree. The Ranger Candaith has asked you to recover a hidden cache of supplies he prepared some time ago, as he will have need of its contents on the journey of the Grey Company.\n3\tTalk to Orskdulug at Amon Sûl\tCandaith's hidden cache at Echad Sûl seems to be gone, and an unsavoury gentleman stands there instead. Candaith sent you to recover a cache of supplies, but it may now be missing.\n4\tReturn to Candaith with the equipment you took from Orskdulug\tCandaith is at his camp below Weathertop, in the Lone-lands. You have recovered the supplies from the hidden cache that were taken by Orskdulug and ruined his plan to rob you with them.\n",
[3062]="7004729F\n1\tTalk to King Elessar in his throne room\tKing Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.\n2\tFind the dwarf delegation in Minas Tirith\tThe delegation of dwarves is on the north-east side of the Fifth Circle in Minas Tirith.\n3\tTalk to Hálsi of the delegation from Erebor\030Talk to Vígmath of the delegation from Erebor\tThe emissaries from Erebor are on the north-east side of the Fifth Circle in Minas Tirith.\n4\tFind the Elf delegation to Minas Tirith\tThe delegation of Elves are just north of the prow, in the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.\n5\tTalk to Olphadon of the delegation from Lórien\030Talk to Lalornil of the delegation from Lórien\tThe delegation of Elves are just north of the prow, in the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.\n6\tFind the Haradrim delegation to Minas Tirith\tThe delegation of Haradrim is on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.\n7\tTalk to Hasong of the delegation from Harad\030Talk to Mauthoi of the delegation from Harad\tThe delegation of Haradrim is on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.\n8\tTalk to King Elessar in his throne room\tKing Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.\n",
[3063]="7004728F\n1\tTalk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain\tThorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.\n2\tTalk to Dwalin in Thorin's Hall, in Ered Luin\030Talk to Mathi Stouthand at Gondamon, in Ered Luin\030Talk to Hannar at Othrikar, in the North Downs\030Talk to Avar at Gabilshathûr, in East Angmar\030Talk to Bósi in the Twenty-first Hall of Khazad-dûm\tKing Thorin III has asked you to deliver news of his ascension to the throne to the following dwarf-leaders throughout Eriador and the Misty Mountains: Dwalin in Thorin's Hall, Ered Luin. Mathi Stouthand at Gondamon, Ered Luin Hannar at Othrikar, North Downs Avar at Gabilshathûr, East Angmar Bósi in the Twenty-first Hall, in Moria After you have delivered his words to each of these dwarf-leaders, you are to return to the King under the Mountain.\n3\tTalk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain\tThorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.\n",
[3064]="70018F0A\n1\tTalk to Frodo Baggins\tFrodo Baggins is on the crest of the hill of Cerin Amroth with some of the members of his company. Milwen has asked you to speak with Frodo Baggins, one of the eight visitors that has come to Lórien in recent days. The Elf-maiden is certain that news of Eriador will be of interest to him.\n2\tTalk to Samwise Gamgee\tSamwise Gamgee is standing on the crest of the hill of Cerin Amroth next to Frodo. Frodo has asked that you fill him and Sam in on news of Eriador.\n3\tTalk to Meriadoc Brandybuck\tMeriadoc Brandybuck is taking a walk somewhere in the vicinity of the hill of Cerin Amroth, and he may now be resting in a private garden nearby. Frodo and Sam were delighted to see you in Lothlórien and know that Merry will be as well.\n4\tTalk to Boromir\tBoromir is wandering somewhere on the north-west outskirts of the clearing from which Cerin Amroth rises, in the centre of Lórien. Merry has wondered if a conversation with you might cheer up Boromir, who does not seem content with the company's presence in Lothlórien.\n5\tTalk to Gimli\tGimli is on the flet atop the crest of Cerin Amroth, in the centre of Lothlórien. Boromir, a little annoyed at Gimli's growing trust of the Elves, has asked you to speak with the dwarf.\n",
[3065]="7001A979\n1\tFind a coffer in Maudhûl-ulur or Ashúrz Maufulug containing information about Mazog\030Defeat Taughâsh Orcs or goblins in the Mirk-eaves (total: 8)\tTaughâsh Orcs and vile goblins can be found throughout the Mirk-eaves. Coffers that may contain Orc-communications can be found inside the camps of Maudhûl-ulur and Ashúrz Maufulug, south-east of Echad Sirion. Alfirimbes has asked you to search the Orc-fortifications in the Mirk-eaves to learn if the Orcs of Mirkwood have learned of Mazog's presence.\n2\tBring the report for Mazog to Alfirimbes\tAlfirimbes is at Echad Sirion, the camp of the Golden Host in the Mirk-eaves, north of Maudhûl-ulur and Ashúrz-maufulug. You have found a report addressed to Mazog in the coffer of an Orc-leader and should bring it now to Alfirimbes.\n3\tTalk to Lúth Greyhammer at Echad Sirion\tLúth Greyhammer is making his ill feelings known as he wanders about Echad Sirion. Alfirimbes wants you to reassure Lúth Greyhammer that the necessary steps are being taken to ensure the errand of the Hidden Guard is being conducted safely and that Mazog's captivity is not threatened.\n4\tTalk to Alfirimbes at Echad Sirion\tAlfirimbes is at Echad Sirion, cautiously overseeing the defence of the camp. Lúth Greyhammer has demanded that one member of his family be posted as sentry watching the captive Orc-leader.\n",
[3066]="70013AF4\n1\tFind and search the Chamber of Knowledge\030Find and search the Chamber of Wisdom\030Find and search the Chamber of Deep Thought\tThe Chamber of Knowledge, the Chamber of Wisdom, and the Chamber of Deep Thought can all be found somewhere within the Great Delving of Moria. Bósi has asked you to search three ancient store-houses of the Great Delving for pages, tablets, or tomes that will enlighten him about Old Days.\n2\tBring the historical records to Bósi\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving of Moria. You have collected ancient records of Moria from three store-houses in the Great Delving and should bring them to Bósi.\n",
[3067]="7005ACA5\n1\tAid the Dwarves of the Landorrim, Narfanghoth, and Temámir at Zirakazhâr\030Aid the Dwarves of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu at Ashmargathâl\tDwarves of the Landorrim, Narfanghoth, and Temámir can be found at Zirakazhâr on the slopes of Zirakzigil to the north-west of Amdân. Dwarves of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu can be found at Ashmargathâl, far to the north of Amdân on the slopes of Bundushâthur. Dáin has asked you to aid the other Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ. You should aid the dwarves in Amdân, as well as those who have battled to Zirakazhâr and Ashmargathâl.\n2\tTalk to the Iron-folk messenger at Zirakazhâr\030Talk to the Iron-folk messenger at Ashmargathâl\tAn Iron-folk messenger can be found at Zirakazhâr or Ashmargathâl. After aiding the Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ, a messenger of the Iron-folk has arrived bearing urgent news for you.\n3\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Khur Azan\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Khur Azan, the Dim-crossing. After learning of how Hermáth Stormhammer aided the dwarves who battled upon the slopes of Zirakzigil and Bundushâthur, Hermáth Stormhammer interjects and calls your attention to events at Khur Azan, the Dim-crossing.\n",
[3068]="7002161A\n1\tTalk to Golodir\030Talk to Lothrandir\030Talk to Elrohir\030Talk to Radanir\tGolodir, Lothrandir, Radanir, and Elrohir are preparing to depart in and around the stables of Rivendell. Halbarad has asked you to check with several members of the Grey Company about their final preparations.\n2\tTalk to Candaith in Rivendell, outside the gate by the stables\tCandaith is outside the gate by the stables in Rivendell. You have spoken with several of the Rangers of the Grey Company in Rivendell and should now speak with Candaith.\n",
[3069]="7005A6A9\n1\tRemove piles of debris (total: 12)\030Remove broken crates (total: 12)\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should remove broken crates and other piles of debris from Vérnozal.\n2\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n3\tCollect coal (total: 4)\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should collect coal in Vérnozal.\n4\tAdd coal to the braziers (total: 12)\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should add coal to the braziers in Vérnozal.\n5\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n6\tHang Zhélruka banners (quantity: see journal)\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should hang Zhélruka banners in Vérnozal.\n7\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n8\tHang a Longbeard banner in the hall\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should hang a Longbeard banner in Vérnozal as well.\n9\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n10\tComplete a Gundabad Mission with either Scout-master Ausma or Hórin\tScout-master Ausma and Hórin can both be found at Vérnozal in Máttugard. You should complete a Gundabad Mission with either Scout-master Ausma or Hórin.\n11\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n",
[3070]="70049415\n1\tVisit Elrond in Rivendell\tYou should visit Elrond Half-elven. He stands in the library of his house in Rivendell.\n2\tTalk to Elrond\tYou should talk to Elrond Half-elven. He stands in the library of his house in Rivendell.\n3\tVisit Bilbo Baggins\tElrond has suggested you visit Bilbo, who can be found in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House in Rivendell.\n4\tTalk to Lindir\tLindir can be found in the Hall of Fire in Elrond's house in Rivendell. You should ask Lindir how you can help with the preparations.\n5\tHelp packing Elves (total: 8)\tYou should help Elves packing throughout Elrond's house in Rivendell.\n6\tReturn to Lindir\tYou have helped a number of packing Elves and should return to Lindir in Elrond's house.\n7\tTalk to Pethelen outside Elrond's House\tLindir suggested you look for Pethelen outside Elrond's house in Rivendell, to help with more preparations for the journey.\n8\tTalk to Ladrochan, the Stable-master\030Talk to Anornaneth\030Talk to Hammadelen\030Talk to Galdor\030Talk to Dúrvenel\030Gather parcels (total: 10)\tYou should go to Rivendell's Market and gather provisions and goods requisitioned for the journey. You will need to ask among the merchants and artisans and also look for some requisitions left lying around.\n9\tBring parcels to Tordúril\tYou should bring the parcels you gathered to Tordúril in the Rivendell Market.\n10\tCarry the goods down to the Rivendell Forges\tYou should bring the pile of parcels next to Tordúril from the Market down to the Rivendell Forges.\n11\tReturn to Pethelen\tYou should return to Pethelen, before Elrond's house in Rivendell, now that you have gathered the parcels as he asked.\n12\tLady Arwen has asked that you visit her in Imlad Gelair, below the falls in Rivendell.\t\n13\tTalk to Arwen\tLady Arwen has asked that you visit her in Imlad Gelair, below the falls in Rivendell.\n14\tTalk to Eliaril\tArwen and Eliaril stand in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. You should talk to Eliaril, Arwen's maid-in-waiting, and see if you can calm her down.\n15\tTalk to Arwen\tArwen and Eliaril stand in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. Hear Arwen's response to Eliaril.\n16\tFind the books Arwen named (total: 4)\tArwen has asked you to find several books in Elrond's library in Rivendell.\n17\tTalk to Elrond\tYou should check in on Elrond in his library in Rivendell to see if he is ready to talk to you.\n",
[3071]="7001AC56\n1\tTalk to Lenglammel at Gwathrendath\030Talk to Forglinn at Gwathrendath\tLenglammel and Forglinn can be found in Gwathrendath, the Elf-outpost in the depths of the Foundations of Stone, in Moria. Issuriel believes that Gorothúl may have set into motion some evil that might ravage Moria in such a way that even Mazog is seeking another kingdom to rule.\n2\tTalk to Bróin in the Peaceful Path\tBróin is in the Peaceful Path, located off Durin's Way. The Elves in Gwathrendath agree with Issuriel's assessment that Gorothúl set some evil into motion before leaving for Dol Guldur. Bróin should be notified of this, for it concerns the Iron Garrison and may affect his plans for the rescue of Bori.\n",
[3072]="70068530\n1\tSpeak with Aphamâr at Rahâl Ghol in Umbar Baharbêl\tAphamâr, dwelling in the upper ward called Rahâl Ghol in Umbar City, wants to speak with you about your ledger.\n2\tBow to Aphamâr in a show of respect and honour\tAphamâr showed you respect in bowing to your deeds within Umbar. She asks that you accept a gift from the Ledger-keepers and requests that you bow to convey your thanks.\n3\tTalk to Aphamâr\tAphamâr is at Rahâl Ghol, the Upper Ward of the city.\n",
})
